WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.003
Validation helps reduce common JavaScript security issues,

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:07.564
but it must be paired with safe APIs and context-specific controls.

00:00:07.564 --> 00:00:14.198
XSS risk appears when untrusted data reaches an output context without appropriate encoding or safe rendering.

00:00:14.198 --> 00:00:18.759
Validation can reject data that does not fit a field's expectations,

00:00:18.759 --> 00:00:22.491
but output encoding and safe templating are still required.

00:00:22.491 --> 00:00:28.296
Injection risk appears when data is interpreted as part of a query, command, expression,

00:00:28.296 --> 00:00:29.540
template, or protocol.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.101
A validation rule may narrow the accepted input, but parameterized queries,

00:00:34.101 --> 00:00:38.248
safe command invocation, and structured APIs are the primary protections.

00:00:38.248 --> 00:00:41.565
Avoid building sensitive operations by concatenating untrusted strings,

00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:44.467
even when the strings passed basic validation.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:46.955
Prototype pollution, at a high level,

00:00:46.955 --> 00:00:51.516
involves unsafe object handling where input can influence object prototype behavior.

00:00:51.516 --> 00:00:55.663
Validation can help by rejecting unexpected keys, limiting nested structures,

00:00:55.663 --> 00:00:57.321
and controlling merge behavior.

00:00:57.321 --> 00:00:58.980
Mass assignment is related:

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.541
if request data is copied directly into objects or database records,

00:01:03.541 --> 00:01:06.858
users may set properties they should not control.

00:01:06.858 --> 00:01:07.508
Node.

00:01:07.508 --> 00:01:11.655
js applications also need to consider path traversal, command injection,

00:01:11.655 --> 00:01:14.557
unsafe deserialization patterns, and insecure file uploads.

00:01:14.557 --> 00:01:19.118
Validation should normalize paths, constrain filenames, check file metadata, limit sizes,

00:01:19.118 --> 00:01:20.777
and enforce allow-listed fields.

00:01:20.777 --> 00:01:23.265
Still, validation is only one layer.

00:01:23.265 --> 00:01:26.167
Safe filesystem APIs, authorization, sandboxing where appropriate,

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.420
and careful output handling remain necessary.
